      "content": "thanks, that helps a lot. i'm trying to see if i can make this argument even more robust for my paper. you mentioned the idea of \"paternalism\" and the \"leadership role.\" could you expand on that? specifically, how did they use those ideas to argue that integrating would actually be *damaging* or *unstable* for both groups? like, what was the specific \"logic\" regarding how integration would lead to social chaos or the loss of group stability? i want to get the nuance of their \"pro-stability\" stance right.",
